<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  TEMPLATE — not a working plist. `install-memo-sweep.sh` fills the @PLACEHOLDERS@ with this
  machine's absolute paths and installs the result. A committed plist with real paths would be
  a lie on any other machine (and would hardcode one person's $HOME), which is exactly the
  mistake the backup installer avoids by generating its plist too.

  Runs `slim memos` every 5 minutes (StartInterval 300) and once at load/login (RunAtLoad),
  so a memo that synced while the timer was between ticks still gets swept on the next wake.

  @CONTAINER@ is the folder the macOS Shortcut EXPORTS INTO — not Apple's Voice Memos
  container, which stays TCC-protected and unreadable to any interpreter (that is the whole
  point of the Shortcut: the file picker grants access by user consent, so no Full Disk
  Access is needed anywhere). Validated headless on 2026-07-20: `shortcuts run` from a
  non-GUI shell really does execute, so this timer works.

  ⚠ Two things measured the hard way that day, both of which look like a broken timer:
   - A memo appears in the Voice Memos APP before its audio downloads. iCloud syncs the
     database entry first, so the app lists a recording whose .m4a is not yet on disk, and
     nothing can copy a file that is not there. The sweep is idempotent and content-addressed,
     so it simply picks the memo up on a later tick — which is why this runs on a schedule
     instead of expecting a memo the instant it is recorded.
   - If the Shortcut's "Save File" destination is left at its default, exports land in
     Shortcuts' own iCloud folder rather than the intended one, and the sweep finds nothing
     while the Shortcut reports success. Set the destination explicitly, and turn ON
     "Overwrite If File Exists" or every run appends -2, -3, -4… (171 copies accumulated
     before this was spotted).
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>@LABEL@</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>@RUNNER@</string>
    </array>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>@UV_DIR@:@FFMPEG_DIR@:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>@REPO_ROOT@</string>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>300</integer>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>@LOG@</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>@LOG@</string>
</dict>
</plist>
